  "helpPairingSection": "Pairing",
  "@helpPairingSection": {
    "description": "Help section title."
  },
  "helpPairingLede": "Pair once; payment files and invoices with that contact are sealed.",
  "@helpPairingLede": {
    "description": "Help section lede."
  },
  "helpPairWhatTitle": "What pairing is",
  "@helpPairWhatTitle": {
    "description": "Topic 1 title."
  },
  "helpPairWhatShort": "Pair once with someone; after that, payment files and invoices between the two wallets are sealed.",
  "@helpPairWhatShort": {
    "description": "Topic 1 lede."
  },
  "helpPairWhatP1": "Pairing links two wallets once: in person by scanning each other’s code, or online with an invite link or five pairing words. Each wallet keeps a key made for that one contact; nothing about it is shared with the Epicbox server.",
  "@helpPairWhatP1": {
    "description": "Topic 1."
  },
  "helpPairWhatP2": "After pairing, a payment file to that contact is **sealed**: only their wallet can open it, and it cannot be changed or forged on the way. Payments over Epicbox between people keep working as before.",
  "@helpPairWhatP2": {
    "description": "Topic 1."
  },
  "helpPairWhatStep1": "Open [[Contacts]] and choose **Pair**.",
  "@helpPairWhatStep1": {
    "description": "Topic 1 step."
  },
  "helpPairWhatStep2": "In person: show your code, scan theirs. Online: send the invite, or read out the pairing words.",
  "@helpPairWhatStep2": {
    "description": "Topic 1 step."
  },
  "helpPairWhatStep3": "Check the words together, then **They match**.",
  "@helpPairWhatStep3": {
    "description": "Topic 1 step."
  },
  "helpPairWhatP3": "Pairing needs Epic Cash on both sides. A contact that is not paired still gets ordinary payment files and Epicbox payments.",
  "@helpPairWhatP3": {
    "description": "Topic 1."
  },
  "helpPairWhyTitle": "Why check the words",
  "@helpPairWhyTitle": {
    "description": "Topic 2 title."
  },
  "helpPairWhyShort": "The four words prove the pairing reached the right wallet and not someone in between.",
  "@helpPairWhyShort": {
    "description": "Topic 2 lede."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP1": "Both wallets show the same four pictures and names after pairing. They come from the two wallets’ keys, so a pairing that someone changed on the way shows different words on the two screens.",
  "@helpPairWhyP1": {
    "description": "Topic 2."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP2": "Compare them on a call or in person, then tap **They match**. The contact becomes **Verified**. **Skip for now** leaves it **Paired, not verified**: payment files are still sealed, but the contact cannot send invoices until the words are checked.",
  "@helpPairWhyP2": {
    "description": "Topic 2."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP3": "If the words differ, tap **They don’t match**. The pairing is dropped on this side. Pair again, in person or with a fresh invite.",
  "@helpPairWhyP3": {
    "description": "Topic 2."
  },
  "helpPairWhyP4": "The word names stay in English in every language, so two people whose wallets use different languages can still compare them.",
  "@helpPairWhyP4": {
    "description": "Help › Pairing › Why check the words: the SAS word names are English on purpose, for comparing across languages."
  },

  "helpPairWordsTitle": "Pairing words",
  "@helpPairWordsTitle": {
    "description": "Topic 3 title."
  },
  "helpPairWordsShort": "Five pictures with names stand in for a link when there is nothing to scan or paste.",
  "@helpPairWordsShort": {
    "description": "Topic 3 lede."
  },
  "helpPairWordsP1": "When one wallet has no camera, or the invite cannot be sent as a link, the inviting wallet shows five pairing words. The other person types their names under **Enter link or words**; the field completes each name after a few letters. The words are good for 10 minutes.",
  "@helpPairWordsP1": {
    "description": "Topic 3."
  },
  "helpPairWordsP2": "The words only find the invite. Whoever has them is in the same position as someone who received the link, so check the four words together afterwards as usual.",
  "@helpPairWordsP2": {
    "description": "Topic 3."
  },
  "helpPairWordsP3": "Pairing words need the Epicbox server. While Epicbox is off, send the invite link instead.",
  "@helpPairWordsP3": {
    "description": "Topic 3."
  },
  "helpPairInvTitle": "Invoices from paired contacts",
  "@helpPairInvTitle": {
    "description": "Topic 4 title."
  },
  "helpPairInvShortDesktop": "Only a Verified contact you allow can ask you to pay. Each request waits for the wallet password.",
  "@helpPairInvShortDesktop": {
    "description": "helpPairInvShort on the desktop, which pays with the wallet password, not a PIN."
  },
  "helpPairInvShort": "Only a Verified contact you allow can ask you to pay. Each request waits for your PIN.",
  "@helpPairInvShort": {
    "description": "Topic 4 lede."
  },
  "helpPairInvP1": "A shop, an exchange or a person you paired can send requests to pay, if you allow it: **Allow invoices** on the contact page, or under [[Settings › Invoices]]. The switch works only for a Verified contact.",
  "@helpPairInvP1": {
    "description": "Topic 4."
  },
  "helpPairInvP2Desktop": "A request shows under [[Invoices › Pay]] with the contact’s name, the amount and a reference. Nothing is paid until you approve it with the wallet password. A request never adds money to your wallet.",
  "@helpPairInvP2Desktop": {
    "description": "helpPairInvP2 on the desktop, which pays with the wallet password, not a PIN."
  },
  "helpPairInvP2": "A request shows under [[Invoices › Pay]] with the contact’s name, the amount and a reference. Nothing is paid until you approve it with your PIN. A request never adds money to your wallet.",
  "@helpPairInvP2": {
    "description": "Topic 4."
  },
  "helpPairInvP3": "Turning the switch off is immediate: new requests from that contact are dropped and open ones are declined.",
  "@helpPairInvP3": {
    "description": "Topic 4."
  },
  "helpPairInvP4": "An exchange that pairs with you deposits and withdraws this way. Deposit: the exchange asks, you approve, the exchange posts. Withdrawal: the exchange sends the payment, your wallet answers on its own, the exchange posts.",
  "@helpPairInvP4": {
    "description": "Topic 4."
  },
  "helpPairRestoreTitle": "What a restore does",
  "@helpPairRestoreTitle": {
    "description": "Topic 5 title."
  },
  "helpPairRestoreShort": "Restoring from the recovery phrase brings every pairing back with the history backup; without it, re-pairing finds the same keys.",
  "@helpPairRestoreShort": {
    "description": "Topic 5 lede."
  },
  "helpPairRestoreP1": "With the history backup, a restore brings every pairing back unchanged: same keys, same Verified marks, same settings. Contacts notice nothing.",
  "@helpPairRestoreP1": {
    "description": "Topic 5."
  },
  "helpPairRestoreP2": "Without the backup, the pairings are gone from this wallet, but the keys are not: they come from the recovery phrase. Pair again with a contact who kept the pairing, and their wallet finds the same keys. It tells them the keys are back, and the contact keeps its Verified mark. On this wallet, Seal payments and Allow invoices start at their defaults.",
  "@helpPairRestoreP2": {
    "description": "Help › Pairing › What a restore does, paragraph 2."
  },
  "helpPairRestoreP3": "A contact sees **Keys changed** only when the phrase is a different one. That can mean a new wallet, or someone else using the name. Check the words again before trusting it.",
  "@helpPairRestoreP3": {
    "description": "Topic 5."
  },
  "helpPairRestoreP4": "Use a pairing on one device at a time. A backup restored on a second device asks before using the contacts there.",
  "@helpPairRestoreP4": {
    "description": "Topic 5."
  },
  "pairNameForCode": "Enter the name they will see, and your code appears here.",
  "@pairNameForCode": {
    "description": "In person, Show my code: the placeholder of the code until the user gave the name the other side sees."
  },
  "pairYourNamePlaceholder": "Your name",
  "@pairYourNamePlaceholder": {
    "description": "Stands for the name in the preview of the invite text until the user types the name they will see."
  },
